      {
         "id": "SECTION_prerequisites",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "<p><span id=\"htZoomImageMsg\"></span></p><div class=\"text-store\" style=\"display:none\"><span id=\"atwaWordRepresent\">Add and represent the result:</span><span id=\"atwaWordMissing\">Add and choose the correct result:</span><span id=\"atwaWordValue\">Value</span><span id=\"atwaWordNewRound\">New practice</span><span id=\"atwaWordAdd\">Add one</span><span id=\"atwaWordRemove\">Remove one</span><span id=\"atwaWordCorrect\">&#10003; Correct!</span><span id=\"atwaWordCongrats\">🎉🎉🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! 🎉🎉🎉<br>You represented the sum correctly!<br>Click '{button}' to practice more!</span><span id=\"atwaWordCongratsChoice\">🎉🎉🎉 CONGRATULATIONS! 🎉🎉🎉<br>You found the correct sum!<br>Click '{button}' to practice more!</span><span id=\"atwaWordTens\">Tens</span><span id=\"atwaWordUnits\">Units</span><span id=\"atwaWordNextStep\">Next step</span><span id=\"atwaWordStepStatus\">Step {current}/{total}</span><span id=\"atwaWordStepCorrect\">Correct! Click 'Next step' to continue.</span><span id=\"atwaWordAbacusStep1\">Step 1: Write the first number <b>{a}</b> in the {units} place.</span><span id=\"atwaWordAbacusStep2\">Step 2: Add <b>{b}</b> in the {units} place. Since {a} + {b} = {sum} reaches 10, carry 1 to the {tens} place: remove the complement <b>{complement}</b> from the {units} place and add <b>1</b> to the {tens} place. The abacus should show <b>{sum}</b>.</span><span id=\"atwaWordAbacusStep3\">Final: {a} + {b} = <b>{sum}</b>. The abacus should show this sum!</span><span id=\"atwaWordAbacusPerfect\">🎉🎉🎉 PERFECT! 🎉🎉🎉<br>{a} + {b} = {sum}<br>Great job using the abacus!</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedQuestion\">The {order} column already holds {base}. Add the bottom digit {added}: type the digit that stays in the column in the result row, and, if the sum reaches ten, type 1 in the carry box above the next order.</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedSquaresLabel\">Addition in this column</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedMsgCarry\">{base} + {added} = {sum}. It reaches 10, so the {order} column keeps {result} and carries 1 to the next order.</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedWrongDigitTen\">That digit is not correct. The column already holds {base} and the bottom digit is {added}. The complement of {base} to ten is {comp}. Since {added} is equal to or greater than {comp}, the ten is completed and 1 is carried to the next order: the squares outside the group of ten are the digit that stays in the {order} column.</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedWrongCarry\">The carry is not correct. Check {base} + {added}: when the sum reaches ten, the carry must be 1.</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedPerfect\">🎉🎉🎉 PERFECT! 🎉🎉🎉<br>{a} + {b} = {sum}<br>Great job!</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedSquaresUsed\">Squares used: {used}.</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedComplementPending\">Complement of {base} to ten: {comp}. Squares still missing to complete the ten: {missing}.</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedComplementUsed\">Complement of {base} to ten: {comp}. Squares that completed the ten: {comp}; squares outside the ten: {outside}.</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedNewProblem\">New problem</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedDigitAria\">Digit that the column keeps</span><span id=\"atwaWordTypedCarryAria\">Carry to the next order</span></div>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "### Prerequisites\n\nIn this class we practice addition with the same tools that humanity created to count. No previous skill is required: we only add two numbers between 1 and 9, and the result is always 10 or more, so every round practices the carry. Before starting, we suggest studying:\n\n- **Running Among the Numbers**: how addition works with larger numbers, using an analogy from Mesoamerican architecture and a step-by-step method for adding numbers of any size (<htcite0>)\n- **Advancing an Order and the Complement**: the rule of advancing an order (carrying over) and the complement to 10 (<htcite1>)\n- **Carry or Not Carry? (Game)**: a game to decide, column by column, whether the sum carries 1 to the next order (<htcite2>)\n- **Practicing addition**: an exercise to practice addition column by column with squares and the complement to 10 (<htcite3>)\n- **Practicing addition with typed values**: the same vertical addition with the digit kept in each column typed in, with numbers generated at random (<htcite4>)",
               "source": [
                  {
