      {
         "id": "SECTION_mathematics",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### The Evolution of Mathematics\n\nAddition appeared in every culture because it comes from the same human act of grouping. Different peoples wrote the result with bones, knots, dots, markers or beads, and each tool organized the count in its own way (<htcite0>; <htcite1>; <htcite2>). In this class we focus on the moment when the result reaches ten, because that is where the carry appears.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "8fe2026a-08b0-4297-b480-cb76d11dfa0f",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "The Order of Addition",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2025",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "687a38b5-de0e-4d16-a4d0-8ec87a545ccb",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Running Among the Numbers",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4caa9fe-de1e-49c5-92de-50ed9c22a42d",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Practicing addition",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
