      {
         "id": "SECTION_carry",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Remembering the Carry and the Complement of 10\n\nBefore using the tools, let us remember the two ideas that make addition work.\n\nThe **complement to 10** of a digit is how much is still missing to reach ten. The complement of 9 is 1, the complement of 6 is 4, and the complement of 5 is 5.\n\nWhen the sum reaches ten, we group those ten units into one unit of the next order. That group is the **carry**, also called *advancing an order*. The digit that stays in the column is what is left outside the group of ten.\n\n**Example: 9 + 3.** The complement of 9 is 1. Since 3 is greater than or equal to 1, the ten is completed: we carry 1 to the next order and 2 remain. Therefore, 9 + 3 = 12.\n\n<div class=\"htAddSquares\"><span class=\"htAddTenGroup\"><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareBase\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareAdded\"></span></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareAdded\"></span><span class=\"htAddSquare htAddSquareAdded\"></span></div>\n<span class=\"htAddSquaresCaption\">9 + 3 = 12</span>\n<span class=\"htAddSquaresNote\">The dashed group is the ten: it becomes the 1 carried to the next order. The 2 squares outside the group stay in the units column.</span>\n\nIn every game on this page the two numbers are between 1 and 9 and their result is always 10 or more. This way, every round practices the carry and the complement of 10 (<htcite0>; <htcite1>; <htcite2>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Advancing an Order and the Complement",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "687a38b5-de0e-4d16-a4d0-8ec87a545ccb",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Running Among the Numbers",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "5539096c-dd7d-4f9c-a137-f0465725b9f4",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Carry or Not Carry? (Game)",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<p><center><div class=\"first_steps_reflection_parent\"><div class=\"first_steps_reflection question_mark\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-brain\"></i></div><div class=\"first_steps_reflection\"><b>Reflection 1: Why does the carry appear?</b><br /><br />When the sum reaches ten, why do we group ten units into one unit of the next order?<br /><br />What would happen if we never made that group?</div></div></center></p>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_africa",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In Africa: Adding with Bones\n\nThe first counting marks we know of were made on bones. To add, people did not need a new tool: they simply kept marking. Thousands of years ago we did not have the concept of carry, therefore, people continued doing continuous marks. To add 9 + 3, they made 12 marks one after another; they did not group ten marks into a new ten (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and place on the bone the total number of marks. The raised fingers show the two numbers; count all the fingers and then make one continuous mark for each unit of the result.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4caa9fe-de1e-49c5-92de-50ed9c22a42d",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Practicing addition",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "687a38b5-de0e-4d16-a4d0-8ec87a545ccb",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Running Among the Numbers",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"atw-game\" data-atw=\"bones\"><p><div class=\"htBoneWrap\"><p class=\"htBonePrompt\" id=\"htBonePrompt\">Add the two numbers, count the raised fingers and place the total number of marks on the bone. <span id=\"atwaBoneEquation\" class=\"atw-target\"></span></p><table class=\"htBoneTable\"><thead><tr><th>Raised fingers</th><th>The bone</th><th>Arrows</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td class=\"htBoneHandsCell\"><div class=\"htBoneHands\" id=\"htBoneHands\"></div></td><td class=\"htBoneBoneCell\"><div class=\"htBone\" id=\"htBone\"><div class=\"htBoneFill\"><span id=\"htBoneMarks\"></span></div></div></td><td class=\"htBoneArrowCell\"><div class=\"htBoneArrows\"><button type=\"button\" class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-up htBoneArrow htBoneArrowUp\" id=\"htBoneAdd\" aria-label=\"Add one\"></button><button type=\"button\" class=\"fa-solid fa-caret-down htBoneArrow htBoneArrowDown\" id=\"htBoneRemove\" aria-label=\"Remove one\"></button></div></td></tr></tbody></table><p class=\"atwa-note\">Thousands of years ago we did not have the concept of carry. Therefore, people continued doing continuous marks: to add 9 + 3 they made 12 marks, one after another, without grouping ten into a new order.</p><p style=\"display: flex; gap: 8px; align-items: center; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap;\"><button type=\"button\" id=\"htBoneNewNumber\" class=\"reset-tutor-btn\">New practice</button> </p><p id=\"htBoneCongrats\" class=\"htBoneCongrats\" style=\"display: none;\"><i class=\"fa-solid fa-medal\" style=\"color: gold;\"></i> Congratulations! The marks on the bone match the sum! <i class=\"fa-solid fa-medal\" style=\"color: gold;\"></i></p><p class=\"desc\">The arrows beside the bone add or remove marks.</p><span id=\"atwaBoneHandAltTpl\" class=\"text-store\">Hand with {n} raised fingers</span></div></p></div>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_quipu",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In America: Adding with Quipus\n\nThe quipu writes numbers vertically on a hanging cord: the units are at the bottom and the tens are stacked above. A knot in the units order is worth 1; when the units order reaches ten knots, those ten are removed and one knot is placed in the tens order above. The result appears as one knot in the tens order and the remaining knots in the units order (<htcite0>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers. Place knots in the **Units** order at the bottom of the cord; when it reaches ten knots, the game removes them and adds one knot to the **Tens** order above. Then continue with the units until you reach the result.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4caa9fe-de1e-49c5-92de-50ed9c22a42d",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Practicing addition",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"atw-game\" data-atw=\"quipu\"></div>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_mesoamerica",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In America: Adding with Mesoamerican Numbers\n\nIn the Mesoamerican system a dot is worth 1 and a bar is worth 5. To add, the result is written with as many bars and dots as needed; after reaching ten, two bars already represent ten (<htcite0>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and represent the result with dots and bars. Since the result is 10 or more, you will use at least two bars.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "68ecf470-69b8-4fcb-b5f8-36f7ee5aee66",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Mesoamerican sums",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"atw-game\" data-atw=\"meso\"></div>",
               "source": null,
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "html",
               "PostMention": ""
            }
         ]
      },
      {
         "id": "SECTION_europe",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In Europe: Adding with Calculi\n\nThe calculi organize the count by place value. Adding on the calculi means placing the total in the correct columns: markers below the bar are worth 1 and markers above the bar are worth 5 (<htcite0>; <htcite1>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and follow the steps shown below the calculi: first write the first number, then add the second and carry 1 to the tens column. Remember that the result is 10 or more, so the tens column will always receive a marker.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "a4caa9fe-de1e-49c5-92de-50ed9c22a42d",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Practicing addition",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  },
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "cabc9843-35ef-4e4f-92fd-17eda864b55e",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
                     "page": "Advancing an Order and the Complement",
                     "date_time": {
                        "type": "gregory",
                        "year": "2026",
                        "month": "",
                        "day": ""
                     }
                  }
               ],
               "date_time": null,
               "isTable": false,
               "imgdesc": "",
               "format": "markdown",
               "PostMention": ""
            },
            {
               "text": "<div class=\"atw-game\" data-atw=\"calculi\"><style>.roman-abacus-container { background: linear-gradient(145deg, #c98a4b, #9c5a26); border-radius: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3rem); box-shadow: 0 20px 35px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.3), inset 0 1px 3px rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.55); padding: clamp(0.8rem, 3vw, 1.6rem) clamp(1rem, 4vw, 2rem); width: 100%; max-width: 680px; margin: 0 auto; box-sizing: border-box; } .roman-abacus-frame { background: #e9dcb4; border-radius: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.6rem); padding: clamp(8px, 2vw, 14px); box-shadow: inset 0 0 0 2px #fbe9c4, inset 0 0 0 5px #6d451f, 0 8px 18px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.2); } #romanAbacusCanvas { display: block; margin: 0 auto; border-radius: 10px; box-shadow: 0 2px 6px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25); cursor: pointer; background-color: #efe1bd; width: 100%; height: auto; aspect-ratio: 700 / 460; max-width: 680px; } .roman-abacus-panel { margin-top: clamp(0.8rem, 4vw, 1.6rem); background: #4a2c12; border-radius: 50px; padding: clamp(8px, 2vw, 12px) clamp(12px, 3vw, 22px); display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: center; flex-wrap: wrap; gap: 12px; box-shadow: inset 0 2px 3px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.5), 0 3px 6px rgba(255, 240, 180, 0.25); } .roman-abacus-panel-left { display: flex; flex-direction: column; align-items: flex-start; gap: 6px; flex: 1 1 200px; min-width: 0; } .roman-abacus-readout { background: #f8efd4; padding: 0.3rem 1rem; border-radius: 30px; font-family: 'Courier New', 'SF Mono', monospace; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 4.6vw, 1.35rem); color: #33190a; box-shadow: inset 0 1px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.12), 0 1px 2px #fff; white-space: nowrap; } .roman-abacus-readout-roman { color: #8a3c10; white-space: normal; overflow-wrap: anywhere; } .roman-abacus-success { background: #2f6b1f; color: #eaffd9; font-weight: bold; padding: 0.35rem 1rem; border-radius: 30px; font-size: clamp(0.85rem, 4vw, 1.1rem); display: none; visibility: hidden; white-space: nowrap; } .roman-abacus-reset { background: #7a4a24; border: none; color: #ffe9c2; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(0.85rem, 4vw, 1.15rem); font-family: inherit; padding: 0.5rem 1.1rem; border-radius: 50px; cursor: pointer; box-shadow: inset 0 -2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35); } .roman-abacus-reset:hover { background: #91592e; } .roman-abacus-game-area { margin-top: clamp(0.8rem, 3vw, 1.3rem); text-align: center; } .roman-abacus-game-label { font-weight: bold; color: #3c200d; margin-right: 0.6rem; font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 4.5vw, 1.2rem); } .roman-abacus-game-target { display: inline-block; background: #ffe9c2; border: 2px solid #7a4a24; border-radius: 20px; padding: 0.25rem 1.1rem; font-family: 'Courier New', 'SF Mono', monospace; font-weight: bold; font-size: clamp(1rem, 5vw, 1.6rem); color: #33190a; } .roman-abacus-congrats { background: #2f6b1f; color: #eaffd9; font-weight: bold; margin-top: 0.9rem; padding: 0.6rem 1rem; border-radius: 20px; text-align: center; font-size: clamp(0.9rem, 4vw, 1.15rem); box-shadow: inset 0 2px 4px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.25); } .roman-abacus-overline { text-decoration: overline; } #romanAbacusFeedback { text-align: center; }</style><div class=\"roman-abacus-container\"><div class=\"roman-abacus-frame\"><canvas id=\"romanAbacusCanvas\" width=\"700\" height=\"460\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"application\" aria-label=\"Roman abacus interactive canvas\" style=\"width:100%; height:auto; max-width:680px; aspect-ratio:700/460\"></canvas></div><div class=\"roman-abacus-panel\"><div class=\"roman-abacus-panel-left\"><div class=\"roman-abacus-readout\">Indo-Arabic: <span id=\"romanAbacusValue\">0</span></div><div class=\"roman-abacus-readout roman-abacus-readout-roman\">Roman: <span id=\"romanAbacusRoman\"></span></div><div id=\"romanAbacusSuccess\" class=\"roman-abacus-success\">&#10003; Correct!</div></div><button id=\"romanAbacusResetBtn\" class=\"roman-abacus-reset\">&#8634; New practice</button></div></div></div>",
