      {
         "id": "SECTION_china",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### In Asia (China): Adding with the Suanpan\n\nOn the suanpan, each column represents a place value. To add, move the beads until the columns show the total, carrying one bead to the next column when a column reaches ten (<htcite0>).\n\n#### The Game\n\nAdd the two numbers and follow the steps shown below the suanpan: first write the first number, then add the second and carry 1 to the tens column. The result is always 10 or more, so the tens column will not stay empty.",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
                     "uuid": "20fe6243-9d1b-44bf-8357-e715cf88d820",
                     "text": "History Tracers Team",
