      {
         "id": "SECTION_conclusion",
         "text": [
            {
               "text": "### Conclusion\n\nIn this class we used the same tools that humanity created to count, but now to add. In every game the result was 10 or more, so we practiced the carry and the complement of 10 again and again.\n\nThe tools change from one culture to another, but the idea is the same: when ten units are completed, they become one unit of the next order. Understanding this lets us add with bones, knots, dots, markers or beads — and also with the numerals we write on paper.\n\nIn the next classes, we will continue practicing addition with larger numbers (<htcite0>).",
               "source": [
                  {
                     "type": 1,
